   "solution": "<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Not available</p><div class=\"source-solutions\" data-answer-source=\"solution_only\"><section><h4>Source solution 1 <small>(score: 1)</small></h4><a name=\"477391\"></a><div itemprop=\"text\">If a minterm is covered by only one prime implicant, that prime implicant is said to be essential, and must be included in the minimum sum of products (SOP)<br>\n<br>\nhere in Kmap all 1's in cell represent minterm and each 1(minterm) not covered by any of prime implicant so these are actually EPI.<br>\n<br>\nand all EPI must be included in minimal SOP. so 7 is the ans<br>\n<br>\n<a href=\"http://ece.gmu.edu/~clorie/Spring11/ECE-301/Lectures/Lecture_8.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">http://ece.gmu.edu/~clorie/Spring11/ECE-301/Lectures/Lecture_8.pdf</a></div></section><section><h4>Source solution 2 <small>(score: 0)</small></h4><a name=\"540243\"></a><div itemprop=\"text\">None of the cells containing 1 are adjacent, that leaves no room for simplification. That means it leaves in same 7 terms.</div></section></div><p><a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/477368\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Official discussion page</a></p>",
